# Paths the merger may fix at land time without a new review (one glob per line): a conflict in a list file or
# a README, a missing doc line. `tools/land.sh --fix` refuses anything else as needing a PASS. A glob is matched one
# path component at a time: `*` stays inside one, `**` stands for any number of whole ones. Whatever this
# says, a file agents read as instructions (CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, .claude/, skill/) always needs a PASS
# (handline/infra/housekeeping.py). land.sh reads main's copy of this file, never the branch's.
**/README.md
docs/**/*.md
design/**/*.md
go/conformance-*.txt
